{
  "comment": "The vectors pinning what model/chat@1 lets a caller set per brain (Prima.Model): the options describe declares, a chat request's session and options, and a chat response's session. option_kinds are the kinds an option may be. valid_describes are describe answers whose options read as they are (absent reads as none); invalid_describes are refused naming member, the first member that breaks the option shape (options[i] for the entry, options[i].<member> for one of its members, an unknown member by its own name). valid_chat_requests and invalid_chat_requests are requests checked against declared, the options a describe declared; a request's other members are the catalyst's to read and are not checked here. valid_chat_responses are chat answers, a response's data or a refusal's error object, and answer session (null for none); invalid_chat_responses are refused naming member, an unknown_session refusal that names a session among them. Read by apps/prima/test/prima/model_test.exs. The further messages of a running chat (Prima.Model.check_input/1): max_input_bytes, max_input_blocks and input_media_types are the input's bounds and the media types an attachment may be; valid_inputs read as they are, each naming kinds, the block kinds it carries, which a harness catalyst writes only when it takes every one of them and refuses otherwise; invalid_inputs are refused naming member, the first member that breaks the input (id, content, content[i] for a block, content[i].<member> for one of its members, an unknown member by its own name when it is a plain word of lowercase letters and underscores and by the member holding it otherwise, input for one that is not an object, content for one past max_input_bytes). A case may give generate in place of input: {id, text_blocks: n} is n blocks {type: text, text: x}, and {id, text_bytes: n} is a string content of n bytes of a; an input's JSON is counted with its members in the order of their names and nothing escaped.",
